<title>USA: COMEX lowers gold futures margins from Sept 9.</title>
<headline>COMEX lowers gold futures margins from Sept 9.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-09-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Deposit margin requirements on the New York Mercantile Exchange's COMEX Division gold futures contracts will be lowered at the close of business on Monday, September 9, the exchange said Friday.</p>
<p>The margins will be decreased to $750 from $1,000 for clearing members, regular members, and hedgers.</p>
<p>Margins for speculators will be lowered to $1,013 from $1,350, the exchange said.</p>
<p>--New York Commodities Desk, +1-212-859-1641.</p>
</text>
